    "title": "Digital Dice: Roll the Luck Machine!",
    "description": "Build your own electronic dice using a 7-segment display. Press a button to generate a random number between 1 and 6, just like rolling a real dice. This experiment introduces 7-segment displays, random number generation, arrays, and controlling multiple output pins simultaneously.",
    "code": "/*\n * EXPERIMENT 5: Digital Dice - Roll the Electronic Luck Machine!\n * EZCirkit Learning Kit\n *\n * COMMON CATHODE 7-Segment Display\n * COM pins -> GND\n * Segment ON  = HIGH\n * Segment OFF = LOW\n */\n\nconst int SEG_A = 2;\nconst int SEG_B = 3;\nconst int SEG_C = 4;\nconst int SEG_D = 5;\nconst int SEG_E = 6;\nconst int SEG_F = 7;\nconst int SEG_G = 8;\n\nconst int BUTTON_PIN = 9;\n\nint segments[] = {\n  SEG_A,\n  SEG_B,\n  SEG_C,\n  SEG_D,\n  SEG_E,\n  SEG_F,\n  SEG_G\n};\n\nconst int numSegments = 7;\n\n/*\n   Digit Patterns\n   Order: A B C D E F G\n   HIGH = ON\n   LOW  = OFF\n*/\n\nbool digits[6][7] = {\n\n  //1\n  {LOW, HIGH, HIGH, LOW, LOW, LOW, LOW},\n\n  //2\n  {HIGH, HIGH, LOW, HIGH, HIGH, LOW, HIGH},\n\n  //3\n  {HIGH, HIGH, HIGH, HIGH, LOW, LOW, HIGH},\n\n  //4\n  {LOW, HIGH, HIGH, LOW, LOW, HIGH, HIGH},\n\n  //5\n  {HIGH, LOW, HIGH, HIGH, LOW, HIGH, HIGH},\n\n  //6\n  {HIGH, LOW, HIGH, HIGH, HIGH, HIGH, HIGH}\n\n};\n\nvoid clearDisplay() {\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < numSegments; i++) {\n    digitalWrite(segments[i], LOW);\n  }\n\n}\n\nvoid showDigit(int number) {\n\n  if (number < 1 || number > 6)\n    return;\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < numSegments; i++) {\n    digitalWrite(segments[i], digits[number - 1][i]);\n  }\n\n}\n\nvoid rollAnimation(int finalNumber) {\n\n  Serial.println(\"Rolling...\");\n\n  for (int cycle = 0; cycle < 15; cycle++) {\n\n    int show = (cycle % 6) + 1;\n\n    showDigit(show);\n\n    if (cycle < 5)\n      delay(150);\n    else if (cycle < 11)\n      delay(60);\n    else\n      delay(130);\n  }\n\n  showDigit(finalNumber);\n\n  Serial.print(\"Rolled: \");\n  Serial.println(finalNumber);\n\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < numSegments; i++) {\n    pinMode(segments[i], OUTPUT);\n  }\n\n  pinMode(BUTTON_PIN, INPUT_PULLUP);\n\n  Serial.begin(9600);\n\n  Serial.println(\"Digital Dice Ready!\");\n  Serial.println(\"Press the button to roll.\");\n\n  randomSeed(analogRead(A3));\n\n  clearDisplay();\n\n  // Startup dash\n  digitalWrite(SEG_G, HIGH);\n\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n\n  if (digitalRead(BUTTON_PIN) == LOW) {\n\n    delay(50);\n\n    int diceRoll = random(1, 7);\n\n    rollAnimation(diceRoll);\n\n    while (digitalRead(BUTTON_PIN) == LOW) {\n      delay(10);\n    }\n\n    delay(100);\n\n  }\n\n}",
    "diagramUrl": "data:image/webp;base64,",
    "pinout": "                     Arduino UNO\n\n           +--------------------------------+\n\n           Pin 2  ●────────330Ω──────── Segment A\n           Pin 3  ●────────330Ω──────── Segment B\n           Pin 4  ●────────330Ω──────── Segment C\n           Pin 5  ●────────330Ω──────── Segment D\n           Pin 6  ●────────330Ω──────── Segment E\n           Pin 7  ●────────330Ω──────── Segment F\n           Pin11 ●────────330Ω──────── Segment G\n\n           5V    ●──────────────────── COM1\n                 │\n                 └──────────────────── COM2\n                 (Common Anode Pins)\n\n           Pin12 ●──────────── Push Button\n                                   │\n           GND   ●──────────────────┘\n\n           +--------------------------------+",
