    "chapterId": "FkNHrAv6t862HjjMMeIg",
    "title": "Servo Motor Angle Control Using Arduino",
    "description": "Control the angular position of a servo motor using Arduino UNO. The Arduino sends control pulses to the servo motor to rotate it to specific positions such as 0°, 90° and 180°. Students learn about servo motors, PWM-style control signals, angular positioning and motor control applications in robotics.",
    "code": "\n#include <Servo.h>\n\nServo myServo;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  myServo.attach(9);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  // Move to 0 degrees\n  myServo.write(0);\n  delay(1000);\n\n  // Move to 90 degrees\n  myServo.write(90);\n  delay(1000);\n\n  // Move to 180 degrees\n  myServo.write(180);\n  delay(1000);\n}\n",
    "diagramUrl": "",
    "pinout": "Servo Red Wire → Regulated 5V supply\n\n\n\nServo Brown/Black Wire → GND\n\n\n\nServo Orange/Yellow Wire → Arduino Digital Pin 9\n\n\n\nConnect external supply GND to Arduino GND when using an external supply.",
