    "chapterId": "FkNHrAv6t862HjjMMeIg",
    "title": "Fire and Flame Detection Alarm",
    "description": "In this experiment, we use a flame sensor to detect fire. When the sensor detects infrared light from a flame, Arduino turns ON the buzzer and LED. The buzzer makes a sound to give an alert. Students learn how a simple fire detection system works.",
    "code": "\nconst int flamePin = 2;\nconst int buzzerPin = 8;\nconst int ledPin = 9;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  pinMode(flamePin, INPUT);\n  pinMode(buzzerPin, OUTPUT);\n  pinMode(ledPin, OUTPUT);\n\n  Serial.begin(9600);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int flameValue = digitalRead(flamePin);\n\n  if (flameValue == LOW) {\n    digitalWrite(buzzerPin, HIGH);\n    digitalWrite(ledPin, HIGH);\n\n    Serial.println(\"Flame Detected!\");\n  }\n  else {\n    digitalWrite(buzzerPin, LOW);\n    digitalWrite(ledPin, LOW);\n\n    Serial.println(\"No Flame Detected\");\n  }\n\n  delay(300);\n}\n",
    "diagramUrl": "",
    "pinout": "              ARDUINO UNO\n          +----------------------+\n          |                      |\n          |  5V ●────────────────┼── VCC (Flame)\n          |  GND ●───────────────┼── GND (Flame)\n          |  Pin 2 ●─────────────┼── DO (Flame)\n          |                      |\n          |  Pin 8 ●─────────────┼── (+) Buzzer\n          |  GND ●───────────────┼── (-) Buzzer\n          |                      |\n          |  Pin 9 ●──[330Ω]─────┼── (+) LED\n          |  GND ●───────────────┼── (-) LED\n          |                      |\n          +----------------------+",
