    "title": "What is Arduino Uno?",
    "description": "Arduino UNO R3 – Description\n\nThe Arduino UNO R3 is an open-source microcontroller development board based on the ATmega328P microcontroller. It is widely used for learning electronics, programming, robotics, automation, and IoT projects.\n\nIt allows users to connect sensors, motors, LEDs, displays, and other electronic components to build interactive projects. It can be programmed using the Arduino IDE through a USB connection.\n\nKey Specifications:\n\n- Microcontroller: ATmega328P\n- Operating Voltage: 5V\n- Input Voltage: 7–12V (recommended)\n- Digital I/O Pins: 14 (6 PWM)\n- Analog Input Pins: 6\n- Flash Memory: 32 KB\n- SRAM: 2 KB\n- Clock Speed: 16 MHz\n- USB Interface:USB Type-B\n\nApplications:\n\n- Robotics and automation\n- Sensor monitoring systems\n- Home automation\n- LED and display control\n- IoT and embedded systems\n- Educational electronics projects\n\nWhy Arduino UNO?\n\nIt is beginner-friendly, affordable, easy to program, and compatible with a wide range of electronic components and modules.",
